<title>UK: UK oil stocks push higher on short squeeze.</title>
<headline>UK oil stocks push higher on short squeeze.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK oil stocks pushed ahead on Wednesday, with investors closing short positions after the FTSE 100 share index defended its rise above the key 4,000 point level, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Oils are having a good run...crude prices have improved recently and we think a few people have been caught short. There's been quite a squeeze,&quot; one market maker said.</p>
<p>Enterprise Oil touched a record 579p before settling back to trade at 575p, up 21p on the day. BP gained 15p to a record 690p and Cairn Energy was up 25p at 400p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
